		{
			title: "Not Everything All At Once"
			icon: "sophisticatedbackpacks:filter_upgrade"
			x: -5.25d
			y: 5.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Vetting Entrance"
			description: [
				"&bA powerful thing to set up early, Bandit, is filtering on your Backpacks!"
				""
				"&bUsing either the Filter Upgrade and/or Create's Filters, you can configure Backpacks to only accept specific items, or specific tags of items."
				""
				"&bAnd with the Void upgrade, you can have a maximum amount of an item before your Backpack will just destroy all excess of that item. Quite handy when you only want a couple stacks of something, like Vault Junk, but not thousands of it."
				""
				"&bIf you have an Upgrade that identifies or changes an item? Say, a Compacting upgrade or an Identification upgrade? And you want those changed items in a different Backpack? Use the Dropper Upgrade! It'll drop all items that match its filter so other bags can pick them up."
			]
			dependencies: ["14C1EE7794D7D6FC"]
			id: "5343D6DE79BF7838"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "215B139A5B4E2EE7"
